 "_caveats": [
  "CSR expenditure in rupees crore, financial years.",
  "Population is Census 2011, the most recent enumerated count India has, because the 2021 census was not held. Per-person figures are therefore CSR now over people counted then.",
  "Jammu and Kashmir's 2011 population includes Ladakh, which became a separate union territory in 2019 and has its own CSR row, so Jammu and Kashmir's per-person figure is somewhat understated.",
  "'PAN India', 'Other Centralized Funds' and 'NEC/Not Mentioned' are CSR the companies did not assign to one state. They are kept separate and are not spread across states.",
  "In 2024-25 the unassigned share falls to about 4 per cent, from between 23 and 44 per cent in each earlier year, and most states' totals rise sharply. The ministry's table does not say why. Treat a state's rise between 2023-24 and 2024-25 as partly a change in how spending was reported.",
  "The ministry revises earlier years as late filings arrive. These are its figures as of 31 March 2026, so 2022-23 here is higher than the 29,988 crore the data.gov.in release of the same year shows.",
  "Per capita income for 2023-24 and 2024-25 is from MoSPI and covers 30 states and union territories. Assam, Haryana and Nagaland have no figure there for those years, so they drop out of the scatter."
 ],
